              "isAccessibleForFree": true,
              "articleBody": "This training article checks the boundaries of the local editorial workflow. It belongs in test fixtures and is not intended for publication.Keeping a draft out of public routesIn the current project, for Russian and English articles selects entries with . The field controls listings, while the direct article route is built separately. A temporary file needs an explicit .This finding comes from the Russian article route and its English counterpart. The prefix excludes some test files from translation checks; it does not itself prevent publication.What the translation hash tracksThe function covers the body and translatable frontmatter: title, description, summary, coverAlt, and FAQ. Changing tags or dates does not change this hash. The algorithm is documented in the hash module.The following example is a fragment to run from the repository root. Its result depends on the supplied file; updating a hash mechanically cannot replace synchronizing the translation.Checks that remain separateA matching sourceHash records which source the translator acknowledged. An editor checks whether the translation preserves its meaning. The editorial package digest covers the exact Russian and English bytes: changing either version invalidates an older review.A build with checks compilation without showing the article page. Visual review needs a separate local project copy and a real Astro preview. If no browser ran, the report keeps .",
